---
description: HTTP handler conventions
globs: src/api/**/*.go
alwaysApply: false
---

Cursor attaches this rule whenever a handler file is in context, so it states
only what a handler edit needs and nothing the repo-wide surface already says.

- Every handler returns `(status int, body any)`; never writes to the response
  writer directly.
- A handler that needs a flag calls the evaluator; it never reads Postgres.
